WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.675
Next, how the line is built, and how to keep it alive.

2
00:00:03.925 --> 00:00:08.450
Three-strand twisted line is easy to splice and stretches well.

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.875
That suits an anchor rode.

4
00:00:11.125 --> 00:00:16.150
Double braid is strong and smooth, and kinder to your hands and your winches.

5
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.475
That suits dock lines.

6
00:00:18.725 --> 00:00:21.300
The great enemy of any line is chafe.

7
00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:27.125
Wherever a line passes through a chock or bends over an edge, protect it with chafe gear.

8
00:00:27.375 --> 00:00:31.625
Rinse the salt out now and then, and store your lines out of the sun.

9
00:00:31.875 --> 00:00:34.200
And here’s the one for the exam.

10
00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:37.925
A knot weakens a line far more than a splice does.

11
00:00:38.175 --> 00:00:39.650
How much?

12
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:43.825
A knot can cost you a third of the strength or more.

13
00:00:44.075 --> 00:00:46.375
A good splice keeps most of it.

14
00:00:46.625 --> 00:00:49.200
So anything permanent gets spliced.
